"2388","On the authority of Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubair ibn Nufair, from his father, that Abu Jubair came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his daughter whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married. The Prophet ﷺ ordered wudu for him and said: ""Perform wudu, O Abu Jubair."" So Abu Jubair began with his mouth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""Do not begin with your mouth, for the disbeliever begins with his mouth."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the wudu water, washed his hands until he cleansed them, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, and the left three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet."
