"2414","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: Salmā, the freed slave woman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or the wife of Abū Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his permission concerning Abū Rāfiʿ, for he had struck her. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abū Rāfiʿ: ""What is between you and her, O Abū Rāfiʿ?"" He said: ""She annoys me, O Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""How did you annoy him, O Salmā?"" She said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I did not annoy him with anything, but he passed wind while he was praying, so I said to him: 'O Abū Rāfiʿ! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has commanded the Muslims that if wind passes from one of them, he should perform ablution.'"" (And al-Ṭabarānī said: ""That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever passes wind should repeat the ablution.'"") So he stood up and struck me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to laugh and said: ""O Abū Rāfiʿ! She only ordered you to do good."""
